r"""
=============================================================================
 EDRC RAILWAY SIGNAL AUTOMATION SUITE  -  MASTER CONSOLE
=============================================================================

 A single front end for every test program in the suite.

 FLOW
 ----
   STEP 1  OEM            ->  HITACHI / SIEMENS / MEDHA / NIPPON /
                              KYOSAN / HIMA
   STEP 2  DATA           ->  UPLOAD TOC, LOAD COORDINATES (NEW / EXISTING),
                              TRACK LIST / TRACK CAPTURE / SAVED TRACK COORDS,
                              LOCK ROUTE, SPL CASE, AUTO THROW POINTS
   STEP 3  PROGRAMS       ->  Tick the programs to run. The tick ORDER is the
                              RUN ORDER (a numbered badge shows the position).
   STEP 4  EXECUTION      ->  Programs run ONE AFTER ANOTHER. Each program
                              finishes and its report is collected into the
                              session folder BEFORE the next one launches.

 REPORTS
 -------
   EDRC_REPORTS\<OEM>\SESSION_<yyyymmdd_hhmmss>\
        01_ROUTE_INITIATION\...xlsx
        02_SIGNAL_CLEARANCE\...xlsx
        SESSION.json          (OEM, data files, run order, results)

 NOTE
 ----
   The individual test programs are NOT modified by this launcher. Each one
   is started as its own process with its own window, exactly as if it were
   opened from PyCharm. The launcher waits for that window to close, picks
   up the Excel report it wrote, then starts the next program.

   The chosen data files are also published to the child process through
   environment variables (EDRC_TOC, EDRC_COORDS, ...) and SESSION.json, so
   the test programs can auto-load them later if you decide to add that.

 Author : EDRC Team
=============================================================================
"""

